meta {
  name: Login
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/login
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: none
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  username: {{username}}
  password: {{password}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

tests {
  test("sets the session cookie", function() {
    expect(res.getHeader("set-cookie"), "no Set-Cookie — login failed").to.not.be.undefined;
  });
}

docs {
  Run this first. Bruno keeps the `user_session_id` cookie in its jar and
  sends it with every other request in the collection.
  
  Set `username` / `password` in the environment to a user you created
  with the CLI (`go run ./cmd/cli`).
  
  Success is `200` + `HX-Redirect: /` + a `Set-Cookie` header, with an
  empty body. Failure is also `200`, with a `FormError` fragment and no
  redirect — the status code never tells you which happened.
  
  ## Edge cases
  
  Change the body and re-send:
  
  | Change | Expected |
  |---|---|
  | wrong `password` | "Incorrect username or password" fragment |
  | `username` that doesn't exist | identical message |
  | both fields removed | identical message |
  
  The identical message for a wrong password and an unknown username is
  deliberate and correct — a different message would let anyone probe for
  valid usernames.
  
  The failing cases do NOT clear the cookie jar, so running them after a
  successful login leaves you logged in. Use **Logout** to actually drop
  the session.
}
